listmonk on FenrirOS
====================

listmonk is a newsletter and mailing-list manager: a single program
(/usr/bin/listmonk, with its web interface and SQL inside) and a PostgreSQL
database. It sends mail through any SMTP server (set in its web settings).
Nothing is configured or running after installation: no configuration, no
database, no admin account.

1. PostgreSQL (13 or newer; install postgresql and start it), as postgres:
       CREATE USER listmonk WITH PASSWORD '<password>';
       CREATE DATABASE listmonk OWNER listmonk;
2. Configuration:
       cp /usr/share/doc/listmonk/config.toml.sample /etc/listmonk/config.toml
       chgrp _listmonk /etc/listmonk/config.toml; chmod 640 /etc/listmonk/config.toml
   and set [db] (user, the password above, database) and [app] address.
   The sample's password "listmonk" is only an example: change it.
3. Create the schema and the admin user (the password is yours to choose):
       cd /var/lib/listmonk
       su -s /bin/sh _listmonk -c 'LISTMONK_ADMIN_USER=admin LISTMONK_ADMIN_PASSWORD=<password> \
           listmonk --config /etc/listmonk/config.toml --install --yes'
   After an upgrade of this package: listmonk --config ... --upgrade --yes
4. Start it: dinitctl enable listmonk (listens on [app] address, by default
   localhost:9000). Uploads go to /var/lib/listmonk/uploads (the working
   directory). To publish it, put nginx in front: an example is
   /usr/share/doc/listmonk/nginx-listmonk.conf.
